Ants are social insects, and the colony is a family community of which every ant is an integral unit.
Apart from the community, any one individual cannot properly function or survive, and the larvae are completely dependent upon the continuous care of the adults.
There are generally three castes, or classes, within a colony: queens, males, and workers.
